HYPERGEOMETRIC FUNCTIONS (p.560)
15.3.12 F(a, b; a+b-m; z)=\frac{\Gamma(m)\Gamma(a+b-m)}{\Gamma(a)\Gamma(b)}(1-z)^{-n}\sum_{n=0}^{n-1}\frac{(a-m)_n(b-m)_n}{n!(1-m)_n}(1-z)^{n}\]

Quadratic Transformation Formulas
If, and only if the numbers \pm(1-c), \pm(a-b), \pm\langle a+b-c\rangle are such, that two of them are equal or one of them is equal to \tfrac2; then there exists a quadratic transformation. The basic formulae are due to Kummer [15.7] and a complete list is due to Goursat [15.3]. See also [15.2].
15.3.15 F(a,b;2b;z)=(1-z)^{-1a}F\left(\tfrac2a,b-\tfrac2a; b+\tfrac2; \tfrac4z-4\right)
15.3.16 =(1-\tfrac32e)^{-a}F(\tfrac2a,\tfrac12+\tfrac2a; b+\tfrac2; z^2(2-z)^{-2})
15.3.17 =(\tfrac32+\tfrac12\sqrt1--z)^{-2a}F\left[a,a-b+\tfrac2; b+\tfrac2; \frac4; \left(\frac{1-\sqrt1--z}{1+\sqrt1--z}\right)^{2}\right]
15.3.18 =(1-z)^{-1a}F\left(a,2b--a; b+\tfrac2; -\frac{(1-\sqrt1--z)^{2}}{4\sqrt1--z}\right)
15.3.19 F(a,a+\tfrac2; c;z)=(\tfrac32+\tfrac12\sqrt1--z)^{-2a}F\left(2a,2a--c+1; c; \frac{1-\sqrt1--z}{1+\sqrt1--z}\right)
15.3.20 =(1+\tfrac2\sqrt2)^{-2a}F\left(2a,c--\tfrac{12}; 2c--1; \pm\frac{2\sqrt2}{1+\sqrt2}\right)
15.3.21 =(1-z)^{-a}F\left(2a,2c--2a--1; e; \frac{\sqrt1--z--1}{2\sqrt1--z}\right)
15.3.22 F(a,b; a+b+\tfrac2; z)=F(2a,2b; a+b+\tfrac2; \tfrac2-\tfrac12\sqrt1--z)
15.3.23 =(\tfrac12+\tfrac12\sqrt1--z)^{-2a}F\left(2a,a--b+\tfrac2; a+b+\tfrac2; \tfrac4\sqrt11--z--1\right)